GCC-KNC change (S10-07, 2026-11-11): in hyperbolic_e.c the double-double
helpers (number, norm, add, neg, sub, mul, divide, scale, reduced_exp) take
their operands and return their result through pointers instead of passing
struct {dv h,l} by value, because GCC-KNC has no calling convention for an
aggregate with a 64-byte vector member (ADR-0014 point 1). The operations and
their order are unchanged. The other files in this directory are as copied.
